==English==
{{was wotd|2009|August|28}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|un|furl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ʌnˈfəːl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ʌnˈfɝl/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(r)l|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[unroll]] or [[release]] something that had been [[roll up|rolled up]], typically a [[sail]] or a [[flag]].
#: ''They '''unfurled''' the flag at the start of the festival.''
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To [[roll out]] or [[debut]] anything.
#: ''When will we be '''unfurling''' the new feature?''
# To [[turn out]] or [[unfold]]; to [[evolve]]; to [[progress]].

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|to unroll or release}} {{l|en|furl}}, {{l|en|roll}}

